WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.339
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.639 --> 00:00:09.246
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:17.028
Unit thirty-three: Advanced Linking: Lest, With a View to. Today you will express purpose and precaution formally.

4
00:00:17.328 --> 00:00:19.678
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:23.785
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.489
Lest.

7
00:00:26.483 --> 00:00:28.796
Lest means in order to prevent something.

8
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:31.197
He ran lest he miss the train.

9
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.203
Your turn. Say: Lest.

10
00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:37.940
Lest.

11
00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:39.684
With a view to.

12
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:42.660
With a view to means with the aim of.

13
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.924
With a view to saving money.

14
00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:47.867
Your turn. Say: With a view to.

15
00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:52.001
With a view to.

16
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:53.879
In the hope that.

17
00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:57.951
In the hope that means wishing that something will happen.

18
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.027
In the hope that you agree.

19
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:03.339
Your turn. Say: In the hope that.

20
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.491
In the hope that.

21
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.448
So as not to.

22
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:13.088
So as not to means to avoid doing something.

23
00:01:13.683 --> 00:01:15.811
Speak quietly so as not to wake him.

24
00:01:16.417 --> 00:01:19.301
Your turn. Say: So as not to.

25
00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.609
So as not to.

26
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.200
Provided.

27
00:01:26.217 --> 00:01:28.379
Provided means on condition that.

28
00:01:28.983 --> 00:01:30.913
Provided you pay, you may enter.

29
00:01:31.517 --> 00:01:33.937
Your turn. Say: Provided.

30
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:37.697
Provided.

31
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.463
Supposing.

32
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.007
Supposing means if, in a hypothetical way.

33
00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:44.989
Supposing it fails?

34
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:47.818
Your turn. Say: Supposing.

35
00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:51.552
Supposing.

36
00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:53.225
Purpose.

37
00:01:54.217 --> 00:01:56.669
Purpose means the reason for doing something.

38
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.760
The purpose of the meeting.

39
00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.095
Your turn. Say: Purpose.

40
00:02:04.933 --> 00:02:05.911
Purpose.

41
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:07.651
Precaution.

42
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.335
Precaution means an action taken in advance.

43
00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.613
A safety precaution.

44
00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:16.625
Your turn. Say: Precaution.

45
00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:20.421
Precaution.

46
00:02:21.233 --> 00:02:24.873
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.717 --> 00:02:30.352
Visal, how do formal writers say He locked the door so that nobody could enter?

48
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:44.911
He locked the door lest anyone enter. Lest means for fear that or to prevent, and it takes the subjunctive base form or should: lest he forget, lest he should forget.

49
00:02:46.017 --> 00:02:47.262
What about aims?

50
00:02:48.350 --> 00:03:02.438
With a view to is followed by a gerund: The company reduced prices with a view to attracting customers. In the hope that is followed by a clause: She waited in the hope that he would call.

51
00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.690
And conditions?

52
00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:16.052
Provided means on condition that: You may borrow it provided you return it. So as not to is a negative purpose: He tiptoed so as not to wake the baby.

53
00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.258
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.117 --> 00:03:26.365
Grammar focus: Purpose and precaution: lest plus base verb and should; with a view to plus gerund.

55
00:03:26.665 --> 00:03:27.841
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:30.422
He ran lest he miss the train.

57
00:03:31.317 --> 00:03:34.373
They cut prices with a view to attracting customers.

58
00:03:35.283 --> 00:03:37.840
She whispered so as not to wake the baby.

59
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.926
Lest takes the base form or should. With a view to takes a gerund. Provided means on condition that.

60
00:03:45.683 --> 00:03:49.218
Be careful! Don't say: He ran lest he missed the train.

61
00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:53.747
Say: He ran lest he miss the train.

62
00:03:54.047 --> 00:03:55.501
Use the base form.

63
00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.347
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:01.297
For Fear That.

65
00:04:01.597 --> 00:04:04.084
He wrote everything down lest he should forget.

66
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.725
The firm cut its prices with a view to attracting more customers.

67
00:04:09.733 --> 00:04:11.884
She waited in the hope that he would call.

68
00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.503
They crept past so as not to wake the baby.

69
00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.720
You may enter provided you show your ticket.

70
00:04:19.833 --> 00:04:23.591
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.426
He ran lest he blank the train.

72
00:04:26.726 --> 00:04:29.706
A, misses. B, miss. C, missed.

73
00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:35.127
The answer is B: miss.

74
00:04:36.283 --> 00:04:38.596
With a view to blank money, she saved.

75
00:04:38.896 --> 00:04:42.550
A, save. B, saving. C, saved.

76
00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.809
The answer is B: saving.

77
00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.508
Provided means blank.

78
00:04:50.808 --> 00:04:55.054
A, on condition that. B, in spite of. C, because of.

79
00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.867
The answer is A: on condition that.

80
00:05:02.017 --> 00:05:04.074
So as not to expresses blank.

81
00:05:04.374 --> 00:05:09.026
A, a negative purpose. B, a result. C, a habit.

82
00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:15.263
The answer is A: a negative purpose.

83
00:05:16.417 --> 00:05:19.856
According to the reading, why did the firm cut its prices?

84
00:05:20.156 --> 00:05:25.400
A, to attract customers. B, to close. C, to hide errors.

85
00:05:28.933 --> 00:05:31.711
The answer is A: to attract customers.

86
00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:36.261
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:37.117 --> 00:05:40.358
Write a formal sentence using 'lest' or 'with a view to'.

88
00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.662
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:50.962 --> 00:06:03.555
She studied every night lest she should fail the exam. The school extended its library hours with a view to helping students prepare. Both structures express purpose in a formal way.

90
00:06:03.855 --> 00:06:05.564
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:14.443
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and purpose and precaution: lest plus base verb and should; with a view to plus gerund.

92
00:06:14.743 --> 00:06:18.533
Today's value is foresight. Prepare today for the world of tomorrow.

93
00:06:18.833 --> 00:06:21.683
See you in Unit thirty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:21.983 --> 00:06:25.065
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

